#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# harmonic_number

#% text
# `harmonic_number(n)` gives the harmonic number H_n = 1 + 1/2 + ... + 1/n.

#% text
# `harmonic_number(n, r)` gives the sum of 1/k^r for k from 1 to n.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# Integers give exact rationals; other numbers use H(x) = digamma(x + 1) + euler_gamma.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
harmonic_number(10)
#% output
#= 7381/2520

#% cell
harmonic_number(3, 2)
#% output
#= 49/36

#% subsection
# Scope

#% cell
harmonic_number(2.5)
#% output
#= 1.680372305546776

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# Large indices are fast (binary splitting):

#% cell
length(integer_digits(denominator(harmonic_number(100000))))
#% output
#= 43450

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `digamma`, `zeta`
